{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"01b24783-2d87-4e75-9b89-4a104a7211fd","agentId":"a1dcd2d766be47a9a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Do not spawn subagents or forks. Do not commit or push. Do not edit anything in C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers except files under docs/vehicles/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/pdf/ and pdf-sources/.\n\nRefresh the one-page Service Hub PDF for a 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T (VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115). Generator: C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\vehicles\\ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\\pdf-sources\\make_hub_pdf.py (reportlab, hand-written CARDS rows). Copy it to the scratchpad C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\ and work there. Run with C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe (has reportlab and pypdfium2; do NOT use the scratchpad pdfenv, it is broken). Update the date in the header to 2026-10-07.\n\nBring every row up to date with the real data; do not invent anything:\n- Read current facts from the code/data: mes-log-mcp/mes/service_specs.py, maintenance_specs.py, drivetrain_specs.py; cuore's service ledger via `from mes import service; service.load(\"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\")` (sys.path add C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp; read-only) to see whether any service records exist now; and the MES workup `from mes import workup; workup.build(vin=\"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\")` for the EVAP / network state.\n- EVAP & emissions row: P0440 returned after clears on 2026-09-28 and 2026-09-29 scans; codes cleared 2026-09-29 (SCAN_2609291046); the 2026-10-04 engine session and scan read clean but both came after the clear, before any monitor re-ran, so the repair is UNVERIFIED. P0455 and P0456 freeze frames were set with fuel above 85 % (EVAP monitor runs at 15-85 %). Open items: wiTECH flash check, Test A (ESIM switch), recalls 25V586000 and 18V636000; do not clear codes; verify with a readiness read after drives with fuel 15-85 %.\n- Network / body / ADAS row: the network and ADAS codes (U0100, U1713, B1040, C141B) were present 2026-09-28 and gone by 2026-09-29: one power/bus event; B1176 (rear left window riser) persisted on 2026-09-29 and is a separate body fault.\n- Keep the maintenance/transfer case DUE items consistent with maintenance_specs/drivetrain_specs (transfer case oil due at 80k mi/128k km/8 yr; drive belt; air filter and plugs at 90k mi; brake fluid every 2 yr) and say \"unless records show it was done\" when no ledger record exists.\n- If any service record now exists in the ledger, show it in \"Last known service\".\nExactly ONE US Letter page. Render to PNG with pypdfium2 via the .venv python and look at it with your Read tool; fix overflow, clipping or a second page. Plain sentences, no em dashes. Output: C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\Stelvio Service Hub (1 page).pdf (overwrite); copy the final PDF and generator back to ...\\pdf\\ and ...\\pdf-sources\\. Report what changed and the page count."},"uuid":"b9d570d1-eb92-495f-a1c4-795631ba368b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T00:07:24.053Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
