{"parentUuid":"a33f62aa-ef0f-4b5b-ac16-cfd8a1bc9dad","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1dcd2d766be47a9a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfooRzScaQV1T6CPutAhm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WgAu1LT7YS1hWSRKFLkyhQ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\make_hub_pdf.py","old_string":"    (\"EVAP & emissions\",\n     \"P0455, P0456, P0440 chronic since 2025-09. System sealed (3 smoke tests); canister, ESIM, cap, filter, \"\n     \"purge valve all new. ECM software 52170619 / P235QB39. P0455/P0456 freeze frames were set with fuel at \"\n     \"92-94%; the EVAP monitor only runs with fuel between 15-85%.\",\n     \"P0440 recurred in the 2026-09-28 and 2026-09-29 scans after earlier clears; codes cleared again 2026-09-29 \"\n     \"10:46 (SCAN_2609291046). The 2026-10-04 engine session and scan read clean, but both came after that clear \"\n     \"and before any monitor could re-run: repair is UNVERIFIED, not confirmed.\",\n     \"wiTECH flash check (TSB 18-030-17), then Test A (ESIM switch in wiTECH). Check recalls 25V586000 (fuel \"\n     \"pump) and 18V636000 (2.0L ECM software). Do not clear codes again; verify with a readiness read after \"\n     \"drives with fuel between 15-85%.\",\n     \"/tree, /dashboard\"),\n    (\"Network / body / ADAS\",\n     \"Network: U0100 (ECM comms), U1713 (BCM), B1040 (RFHUB), C141B (DASM camera blocked) -- chronic since \"\n     \"2026-06-07/08-27. Separate: B1176 (rear left window riser, BCM), chronic since 2026-08-27.\",\n     \"U0100/U1713/B1040/C141B were present in the 2026-09-28 scan and gone by the 2026-09-29 scan: one power/bus \"\n     \"event, not per-module faults. B1176 persisted through the 2026-09-29 scan -- a separate, unresolved body \"\n     \"fault, not part of the network event.\",\n     \"Confirm the network codes stay clear on the next scan. For B1176: grey-cable read of ABS/HALF, then the \"\n     \"window-riser fault tree (do not fold it into the network-cascade steps).\",\n     \"/tree\"),","new_string":"    (\"EVAP & emissions\",\n     \"P0455, P0456, P0440 chronic since 2025-09. System sealed (3 smoke tests); canister, ESIM, cap, filter, \"\n     \"purge valve all new. ECM software 52170619 / P235QB39. P0455/P0456 freeze frames: fuel 92-94% (EVAP \"\n     \"monitor needs 15-85%).\",\n     \"P0440 recurred in the 2026-09-28 and 09-29 scans after earlier clears; cleared again 2026-09-29 10:46 \"\n     \"(SCAN_2609291046). The 2026-10-04 clean session/scan came after that clear, before any monitor could \"\n     \"re-run: repair is UNVERIFIED, not confirmed.\",\n     \"wiTECH flash check (TSB 18-030-17), then Test A (ESIM switch). Check recalls 25V586000 (fuel pump) and \"\n     \"18V636000 (ECM software). Do not clear codes again; verify with a readiness read after drives with fuel \"\n     \"15-85%.\",\n     \"/tree, /dashboard\"),\n    (\"Network / body / ADAS\",\n     \"Network: U0100 (ECM comms), U1713 (BCM), B1040 (RFHUB), C141B (DASM camera) -- chronic since 2026-06/\"\n     \"08-27. Separate: B1176 (rear left window riser, BCM), chronic since 2026-08-27.\",\n     \"Network codes present in the 2026-09-28 scan, gone by 2026-09-29: one power/bus event, not per-module \"\n     \"faults. B1176 persisted through 2026-09-29 -- a separate, unresolved body fault.\",\n     \"Confirm network codes stay clear next scan. B1176: grey-cable read of ABS/HALF, then the window-riser \"\n     \"fault tree (separate from the network-cascade steps).\",\n     \"/tree\"),"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":163962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1196,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard",