{"parentUuid":"1290334f-862e-4ff2-a744-bbb2b7973fdb","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1dcd2d766be47a9a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfooUsn6u36rXsJpHWEgH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G69XUqibz5y2kwBoYe34bF","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Refreshed the one-page Stelvio Service Hub PDF. Output confirmed as exactly 1 page (US Letter), rendered to PNG with pypdfium2 via the .venv python and visually checked for overflow/clipping — none found.\n\nWhat changed (generator: C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\vehicles\\ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\\pdf-sources\\make_hub_pdf.py):\n\n1. Header date updated to 2026-10-07 (subtitle line and module docstring). Torque fact-check footnote date (2026-09-26) left unchanged since that research pass itself wasn't redone.\n\n2. Data pulled fresh from source-of-truth:\n   - cuore service ledger (`mes.service.load(\"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\")`) is still empty — no service records exist, so every \"Last known service\" / \"No record\" cell was left as-is (nothing to show).\n   - `mes.workup.build(vin=...)` confirmed: odometer still 142,289.9 km / ~88,400 mi as of the last reading (2026-09-25); the 2026-10-04 session had no odometer reading.\n   - service_specs.py / maintenance_specs.py / drivetrain_specs.py re-checked against the existing card text — all matched already (oil interval, torques, transfer case 80k mi/128k km/8yr, drive belt, brake fluid 2yr, etc.), so those rows needed no factual changes beyond consistency wording.\n\n3. EVAP & emissions row rewritten: P0440 recurred in the 2026-09-28 and 2026-09-29 scans after earlier clears; codes cleared again 2026-09-29 10:46 via SCAN_2609291046. The 2026-10-04 clean engine session and scan read both came after that clear and before any monitor could re-run, so the row now says UNVERIFIED, not confirmed. Added that the P0455/P0456 freeze frames were recorded with fuel at 92-94% (confirmed from workup freeze-frame data), noting the EVAP monitor only runs at 15-85% fuel. Open items: wiTECH flash check (TSB 18-030-17), Test A (ESIM switch), recalls 25V586000 and 18V636000, do not clear codes again, verify with a readiness read after drives at 15-85% fuel.\n\n4. Network / body / ADAS row rewritten: U0100, U1713, B1040, C141B were present in the 2026-09-28 scan and gone by 2026-09-29 — framed as one power/bus event, not per-module faults. B1176 (rear left window riser) persisted through 2026-09-29 and is now called out explicitly as a separate, unresolved body fault, with its own fault-tree open item (kept apart from the network-cascade steps).\n\n5. Routine maintenance row: added that the car (at ~88,400 mi) is approaching the 90k mi mark for both the air filter and spark plug interval (owner's manual mandatory points every 30k mi), and added \"unless records show these were already done\" language per instructions, consistent with the empty ledger.\n\n6. Tightened body font (7.4→7.0pt) and cell padding slightly to fit the two expanded rows (EVAP, Network) onto the single page without losing content — first render came out at 2 pages, fixed by this plus trimming cell text, then re-verified at 1 page.\n\nNo em dashes used anywhere (checked via grep for U+2014/U+2013) — existing \"--\" style from the original file was kept.\n\nOutput files:\n- C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\Stelvio Service Hub (1 page).pdf (overwritten, 1 page)\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\vehicles\\ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\\pdf\\Stelvio Service Hub (1 page).pdf (copied, 1 page)\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\vehicles\\ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\\pdf-sources\\make_hub_pdf.py (copied, updated generator)\n\nNo other files in mcp-servers were touched. No commits made."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":173131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":444,"ephemeral